n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|   |  \n|  User Experience (UX) is the discipline of designing products, services, and systems that enable users to achieve their goals efficiently, effectively, and with satisfaction.  |  \n|   |  \n|  UX is not only about visual design.  |  \n|   |  \n|  It encompasses:  |  \n|   |  \n|  - Understanding users  |  \n|  - Solving real problems  |  \n|  - Designing interactions  |  \n|  - Improving usability  |  \n|  - Supporting business objectives  |  \n|  - Measuring outcomes  |  \n|  - Continuously improving experiences  |  \n|   |  \n|  A successful UX balances:  |  \n|   |  \n|  • User Needs  |  \n|  • Business Goals  |  \n|  • Technical Feasibility  |  \n|   |  \n|  Good UX minimizes friction while maximizing value.  |  \n|   |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|  2. WHAT IS USER EXPERIENCE?  |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|   |  \n|  ISO 9241-210 defines User Experience as:  |  \n|   |  \n|  \"A person's perceptions and responses resulting from the use and anticipated use of a product, system, or service.\"  |  \n|   |  \n|  UX includes:  |  \n|   |  \n|  - Emotions  |  \n|  - Expectations  |  \n|  - Perceptions  |  \n|  - Behaviors  |  \n|  - Accessibility  |  \n|  - Learnability  |  \n|  - Efficiency  |  \n|  - Satisfaction  |  \n|   |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|  3. UX VS UI  |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|   |  \n|  UX Design  |  \n|   |  \n|  Focuses on:  |  \n|   |  \n|  - Problem solving  |  \n|  - User goals  |  \n|  - Research  |  \n|  - Structure  |  \n|  - Navigation  |  \n|  - Information architecture  |  \n|  - User flows  |  \n|  - Testing  |  \n|   |  \n|  UI Design  |  \n|   |  \n|  Focuses on:  |  \n|   |  \n|  - Visual appearance  |  \n|  - Typography  |  \n|  - Colors  |  \n|  - Components  |  \n|  - Layout  |  \n|  - Icons  |  \n|  - Visual hierarchy  |  \n|  - Brand consistency  |  \n|   |  \n|  UX answers:  |  \n|   |  \n|  \"Does it work well?\"  |  \n|   |  \n|  UI answers:  |  \n|   |  \n|  \"Does it look and feel good?\"  |  \n|   |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|  4. UX MINDSET  |  \n|  ------------------------------------------------------------  |  \n|   |  \n|  Professional UX designers think in systems rather than screens.  |  \n|   |  \n|  Key questions include:  |  \nEnd of preview. Expand in Data Studio⟨43⟩\n* * *\n  *  Previous⟨29⟩\n  * 1⟨44⟩\n  * 2⟨45⟩\n  * 3⟨46⟩\n  * ...⟨47⟩\n  * 146⟨48⟩\n  * Next ⟨45⟩\n\n\nREADME.md exists but content is empty. \nCopy to bucket new\nUse this dataset \n\nDownloads last month\n    74\nNumber of rows: 14,569 Total file size: 252 kB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨49⟩ Privacy⟨50⟩ About⟨51⟩ Careers⟨52⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
